    "learningGain": 0,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "description": "Current developments in the field of Risk Management. Topics vary from semester to semester. May be repeated only if topic is different. NOTE: This course meets on four Saturdays from 9:00 am - 4:30 pm with an hour lunch. Those four Saturdays are: Saturday, March 7, Saturday, March 28, Saturday, April 11, Saturday, April 25. Distressed, Unique, High-Capacity, and Emerging Risk TransferHow do you insure body parts? A priceless art collection? A billion-dollar construction project? A film production during COVID? The surplus lines industry. Born in a coffee house in London in the 1700s, the surplus lines industry insures the tough risks, that is, the unique, the distressed, the high-capacity, and the emerging risks. Given todaybs risk-accretive environment, students will learn the importance of the surplus lines market to risk management for organizations of all types. Industry practitioners featured in nearly all class sessions illuminate the course materials with their practical experience. Ultimately, this course aims to equip students with the skills to think critically about these tough risks and develop innovative solutions to transfer those risks to the surplus lines industry.",
