    "id": "10632",
    "code": "ART-484",
    "title": "Contemporary Issues in Art",
    "credits": 4,
    "professor": "Jennifer West",
    "professors": [
        "Jennifer West"
    ],
    "department": "Art",
    "rating": 0,
    "difficulty": 0,
    "workload": 0,
    "learningGain": 0,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "description": "An advanced studio and discussion course aims to expand a students relationship to, and understanding of, contemporary artistic dissemination, discourse, and display via a series of rotating topics. NOTE:   Recommended Preparation: junior status or permission of instructor. Super-8 and the Hand-Made FilmThis course is a studio class for analog and hand-painted film post the digital revolution in an art context. Students shoot Super 8 film and learn to hand-paint, etch and collage 16mm filmstrips. The class screens historical and contemporary works utilizing analog film processes, read relevant essays for discussion, and learn about the film community. Workshops, demonstrations and a field trip to the film lab push students to experiment with shooting on Super 8 film, using found footage and the unique processes of drawing, painting, staining, scratching and collage directly on filmstrips as well as experimental film processing. Students learn to project their work on film projectors while also transferring their work to digital formats for editing and digital projection. The creative projects, lectures, discussions, works screened, field trips and readings will lead to an understanding of experimental analog film in a digital world.",
    "schedule": "TTh 12:00pm-02:40pm",
    "schedules": [
        "TTh 12:00pm-02:40pm"
    ],
    "prerequisites": [],
    "evaluationMethods": [],
