    "learningGain": 0,
    "reviewCount": 0,
    "description": "Music problems and composers of the period. Specific emphasis to be determined by the department. NOTE: Topic: Realism, Symbolism and Early Modernism in European Music 1870-1910 Course Description: What cultural conditions produced the extraordinary musical repertory which defined the so-called 'Emancipation of the Dissonance' in 1910? This course will explore the beginnings of musical modernism by focusing on ten works, created between 1874 and 1909, which are representative of Realism, Symbolism, early Modernism and the search for a new musical aesthetic. Our approach will vary by region, work and composer, from Bizet and Wagner to Busoni and Skryabin, but will generally involve comparative study of source literature and style analysis. Extensive listening required.",
    "schedule": "Th 02:00pm-03:50pm",
    "schedules": [
        "Th 02:00pm-03:50pm"
    ],
